  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGeneral (November 3, 2026) - Elections - Wapello County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n Wapello County, Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections General\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2015 \n2013 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \n\nGeneral\n\n \nNovember 3, 2026\n General Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n\n \n \nPolls will be open from 7:00 a.m. - 8:00 p.m. \nAbsentee Ballot Information \n \n \n \nOctober 14, 2026 - In-person absentee voting (bring valid ID) begins at the auditor's office and absentee ballots can be mailed out. \n \nOctober 19, 2026 by 5:00 p.m. - Last day to mail out absentee ballots.  \n \n \n\nVoters can use the official Iowa absentee ballot request form. Voters can also write a request on a regular piece of paper – one for each voter and include the following information: \n \n \n \nVoter’s name & date of birth \n \nID# (IA DL #, IA non-operator # or 4-digit pin #) \n \nResidential address \n \nMailing address if different than residential address \n \nElection Date or Type \n \nSignature and date of signing \n \n \n\n  \n \n \n \nSaturday, October 31, 2026, from 9:00 a.m. until 5:00 p.m \n \nNovember 2, 2026 - Last day to vote absentee in-person (bring valid ID). \n \nNovember 3, 2026 by 8:00 p.m. - ELECTION DAY - Deadline to return a voted absentee ballot to the Wapello County Auditor's Office. \n \nPOSTMARKS DON'T COUNT  \n \n \n\nVoter Registration Information \n \n \n \nOctober 19, 2026 by 5:00 p.m. - Voter Pre-registration deadline. \n \n \n\nVoter Eligibility Requirements: \n \n\nTo vote in this election one must be a U.S. citizen, a registered voter in the county in which one lives & be 18 years of age. \n \n\nPre-Registered Voters, Voters who are registering on Election Day, Pending Voters and Voters Changing Precincts on Election Day will need to prove identity and residency by using one or more of the forms below. \n \n\nProof of Identity \n \n\nIowa Driver’s License (not expired more than 90 days) \n \n\nIowa Non-operator’s ID (not expired more than 90 days) \n \n\nU.S. Passport (not expired) \n \n\nU.S. Military or Veteran ID (not expired) \n \n\nIowa Voter Identification Card (must be signed) \n \n\nTribal ID Card/Document \n \n\n(must be signed, with photo, not expired) \n \n\n  \n \n\n                           \n \n\nProof of Residence \n \n\n(must include name and current address and be current within 45 days; may be in an electronic format or on paper) \n \n\nResidential lease   \n \n\nUtility bill, including a cell phone bill \n \n\nBank statement \n \n\nPaycheck \n \n\nGovernment check \n \n\nOther government document \n \n\nProperty tax statement \n \n\n(current within 45 days of final payment date) \n \n\nVoters who are using Election Day Registration procedures and are unable to show ID (or prove residence if required) may have their identities attested to by another registered voter in the precinct or have the right to cast a provisional ballot.  Election Day Registrant attesters must also show ID.   \n \n\nFor further information, contact the Wapello County Auditor’s Office at 641-683-0020 between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday. \n \n\n  \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Results Available on Election Night\n \n \n\n 0/22 Precincts Counted\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \nVoting Locations\n \n\n Adams Township/Blakesburg City/Polk Township \n \n\n Includes: Blakesburg City \n Blakesburg City Hall · 101 State Street · Blakesburg, IA 52536 \n \n\n Agency Township/Agency City/Pleasant Township \n \n\n Includes: Agency City \n Agency Community Center · 102 West Main Street · Agency, IA 52530 \n \n\n Cass Township/Chillicothe City \n \n\n Includes: Chillicothe City \n Chillicothe City Hall · 205 Main Street · Chillicothe, IA 52548 \n \n\n Center Township\n Bridge View Center · 102 Church Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Columbia Township/Eddyville City \n \n\n Includes: Eddyville City \n Eddyville Public Library · 202 Second Street · Eddyville, IA 52553 \n \n\n Competine Township\n Highland Center Township Hall · 9906 Highland Center Road · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Dahlonega Township \n \n\n Entrance 15 \n IHCC - Advanced Technology Center (Entrance 15) · 525 Grandview Ave · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Green Township\n Zion Community Church · 15714 Copperhead Road · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Keokuk Township\n Hickory Grove Community Church · 3929 US Hwy 63 · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 1\n Penn Avenue Free Methodist Church · 820 East Pennsylvania Avenue · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 2\n North Court Baptist Church · 1411 North Court Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 3\n Great Prairie AEA 15 · 2814 North Court Road · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 4\n American Legion · 550 West Main Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 5\n Wapello County Courthouse · 101 West 4th Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 6\n Bridge View Center · 102 Church St · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 7\n Davis Street Christian Church · 202 South Davis Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 8\n Wapello County Rural Fire Department · 714 West Mary Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 9\n Bible Baptist Church · 944 West Willams Street · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Ottumwa Precinct 10\n Life Church · 1957 Albia Rd · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n\n Richland Township/Kirkville City \n \n\n Includes: Kirkville City \n Kirkville City Hall · 101 West Main Street · Kirkville, IA 52566 \n \n\n Washington Township/Eldon City \n \n\n Includes: Eldon City \n Eldon Library Hall · 608 West Elm Street · Eldon, IA 52554 \n \n\n Highland Township\n Highland Center Township Hall · 9906 Highland Center Rd. · Ottumwa, IA 52501 \n \n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n General\n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Wapello County Auditor\n\n Wapello County Courthouse\n \n101 W. 4th St.\n \nOttumwa, IA 52501\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Wapello County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8:00am to 4:30pm \n \nPhone Number\n\n Office: (641) 683-0020 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Wapello County Elections\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
